{
 "slug": "js_temporal_plaintime",
 "course": "js",
 "order": 190,
 "url": "/js/js_temporal_plaintime.asp",
 "title": "JavaScript Temporal PlainTime",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "JavaScript Temporal PlainTime"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The PlainTime Object"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Temporal.PlainTime object is a time object without a date."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It represents an ISO 8601 wall-clock time without a date or time zone."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Example: 10:30:00."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It is useful for opening hours, alarms, and any time-only values."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The Temporal.PlainTime Object"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The Temporal PlainTime object is a time object with no date."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It represents an ISO 8601 wall-clock time without a date or time zone."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Example: 14:30:00."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const date = new Temporal.PlainTime(14, 30);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_plaintime"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Create a PlainTime"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "You can create a PlainTime from a string."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const time = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"14:30\");",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_plaintime_from"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "You can also create a PlainTime using numeric values."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const time = new Temporal.PlainTime(14, 30);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_plaintime"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The parameters are: hour, minute, second, millisecond, microsecond, nanosecond."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Get the Current Time"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "You can get the current local time using Temporal.Now.plainTimeISO()."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const now = Temporal.Now.plainTimeISO();",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_plaintime_now"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Get Time Parts"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "You can read the different parts of a PlainTime value."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const time = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"14:30:15.123\");",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_plaintime_from2"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Add and Subtract PlainTime"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Use add() and subtract()\nto do PlainTime math."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "PlainTime is immutable, so the original value is not changed."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const time = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"14:30\");\n\nconst later = time.add({ minutes: 45 });\n\nconst earlier = time.subtract({ hours: 2 });",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_plaintime_add"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "If the time passes midnight, it wraps around:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "const time = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"23:30\");\n\nconst result = time.add({ minutes: 90 });",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_plaintime_add_2"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Calculate PlainTime Differences"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Use since() and until()\nto calculate PlainTime differences."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Both methods return a Temporal.Duration object."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "// Create two PlainTime objects\n\nconst start = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"09:00\");\n\nconst end = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"17:30\");\n\n// Calculate the difference\n\nconst diff = start.since(end);",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "// Create two PlainTime objects\n\nconst start = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"09:00\");\n\nconst end = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"17:30\");\n\n// Calculate the difference\n\nconst diff = start.until(end);",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_plaintime_since"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript since() and until()"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "All temporal date objects have their own since() method:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "plaindate.since(plaindate)",
    "plaintime.since(plaintime)",
    "plainyearmonth.since(plainyearmonth)",
    "plainmonthday.since(plainmonthday)",
    "plaindatetime.since(plaindatetime)",
    "zoneddatetime.since(zoneddatetime)",
    "instant.since(instant)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "All temporal objects have their own until() method:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "plaindate.until(plaindate)",
    "plaintime.until(plaintime)",
    "plainyearmonth.until(plainyearmonth)",
    "plainmonthday.until(plainmonthday)",
    "plaindatetime.until(plaindatetime)",
    "zoneddatetime.until(zoneddatetime)",
    "instant.until(instant)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "LearnMore:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Temporal Since and Until Tutorial"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The PlainTime compare() Method"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Use Temporal.PlainTime.compare() to compare times."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "// Create two PlainTime objects\n\nconst a = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"08:30\");\n\nconst b = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"14:30\");\n\n// Compare the two objects\n\nresult = Temporal.PlainTime.compare(a, b));",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_plaintime_compare"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The result is:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "-1 if the first time is earlier",
    "0 if they are equal",
    "1 if the first time is later"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Do not use =, <, or > when comparing temporal time."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "All temporal objects have their own compare() method:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Temporal.Instant.compare(instant1, instant2)",
    "Temporal.PlainDate.compare(plaindate1, plaindate2)",
    "Temporal.PlainTime.compare(plaintime1, plaintime2)",
    "Temporal.PlainYearMonth.compare(plainyearmonth1, plainyearmonth2)",
    "Temporal.PlainMonthDay.compare(plainmonthday1 plainmonthday2)",
    "Temporal.PlainDateTime.compare(plaindatetime1,plaindatetime2)",
    "Temporal.ZonedDateTime.compare(zoneddtatime1, zoneddtatime2)",
    "Temporal.Duration.compare(duration1, duration2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "LearnMore:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Temporal Compare Tutorial"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The PlainTime equals() Method"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Use equals() to check if two times are the same."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "// Create two PlainTime objects\n\nconst a = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"14:30\");\n\nconst b = Temporal.PlainTime.from(\"14:30\");\n\n// Compare the two objects\n\nresult = a.equals(b);",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_temporal_plaintime_equals"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Most (*) temporal objects have their own equals() method:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "instant.equals(instant)",
    "plaindate.equals(plaindate)",
    "plaintime.equals(plaintime)",
    "plainyearmonth.equals(plainyearmonth)",
    "plainmonthday.equals(plainmonthday)",
    "plaindateTime.equals(plaindatetime)",
    "zoneddateTime.equals(zoneddtatime)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "(*) Duration has not."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "LearnMore:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Temporal Equals Tutorial"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "When to Use PlainTime"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Opening hours (for example: 09:00 to 17:00).",
    "Alarm clock times.",
    "Recurring daily schedules.",
    "Time input fields (without date and time zone)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "If you need date, use PlainDateTime."
  },
